					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE\n\nIn this example we are using Normalize to get the direction of a randomly generated Float 2 value.\nBy subtracting the Float 2 from the smoothed Float 2 we get the difference between the two: the distance.\n\nBy normalizing the distance we get the direction of the vector.\nNext, we add the normalized vector with the smoothed Float2\nThe result is a line that moves, but stays consistent in length."
					}
				},
